I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and the grant as declared is only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Adding `http-client` to the world would make the component import an interface the graph never grants, so instantiation would fail or the grant would be exceeded. The grant change has to be made in the graph declaration, which is outside these two files. Once the `with` clause includes `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>`, I can add the call. Two things to settle first: the query string would send the input text to an external host, so it needs percent-encoding and a decision about whether that data may leave the system, and the `Selection` input has no single "text" field, so the enrichment key needs defining.

